# Build after changes

When a task changes project files, finish by running:

```bash
npm run build
```

- Run it once, after the edits are done, not after every intermediate save.
- If the build fails, fix the cause and run it again until it succeeds.
- Skip the build only when the task did not change any project files.

# Commit titles

At the end, show the commit title twice, with the same text:

1. For this repository.
2. For `D:\GitHub\Harrix-HTML-Template-dist-history`.

Do not create the commits. Only print both titles.
